<div class="wrap"><div class="reading measure-wrap">
  <p class="mono eyebrow">Privacy</p>
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated 24 November 2026.</p>

  <h2>No cookies, no trackers</h2>
  <p>This website does not use cookies, analytics or any third-party trackers. It keeps two small notes in your own browser, and they are never sent anywhere:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>if you switch between the light and dark theme, your choice, until you clear it;</li>
    <li>that our robot, CREW, has already said hello, so he only introduces himself once. This one is deleted when you close the tab.</li>
  </ul>
  {%- if site.assistantLive %}
  <p>To show whether CREW is answering right now, pages with the contact form load a small status file from our Microsoft Azure storage in North Europe. It holds no personal data. Like any web request it reaches Azure with your IP address, which we don’t log.</p>
  {%- endif %}

  <h2>When you email</h2>
  <p>The “What do you need?” boxes on this site only write an email in your own email app. Nothing is sent until you send it yourself.</p>
  <p>Emails you send to <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> are held by our email provider, Zoho Mail, in its EU data centres. They are used only to reply to you and to do business with you. They are kept for as long as needed for that, and for as long as tax records must be kept.</p>

  {%- if site.assistantLive %}{#- shown once the assistant is built and verified (site.js) #}
  <h2>Our automatic first reply</h2>
  <p>An automatic assistant, CREW, reads new emails sent to {{ site.crewEmail }} and usually replies within minutes with a few first questions. It is not a person: its replies say so, and every reply tells you how to reach a person instead. A person from CuSS follows up within two working days. Emails to {{ site.email }} are read only by people.</p>
  <p>CREW runs on Microsoft Azure, in its North Europe region (Ireland). To write a reply, it sends your email to Claude, an AI model made by Anthropic, through Amazon Bedrock’s European service, which processes it only in the EU. Amazon Bedrock does not use it to train AI models and does not share it with Anthropic. Under Amazon’s terms, it may keep it for a limited time to detect misuse.</p>
  <p>What is kept, and for how long:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your email and CREW’s replies, in the {{ site.crewEmail }} mailbox at Zoho Mail (EU data centres): deleted after 12 months;</li>
    <li>a short record of the conversation (your email address, the subject, a one-line summary, its status and dates), in Microsoft Azure, North Europe: deleted 12 months after the last message;</li>
    <li>a count of the emails from your address each day, to stop floods of messages: deleted after 2 days;</li>
    <li>technical logs showing which email was handled and what CREW did, without its text: deleted after 30 days;</li>
    <li>an alert to our Gmail inbox with your address, your message and CREW’s reply, so a person can follow up: kept until deleted (an alert that can’t go at once waits in Azure until it can). Gmail is run by Google, whose servers may be outside the EU.</li>
  </ul>
  {%- endif %}

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>This website is hosted on GitHub Pages, run by GitHub, Inc. Like any web host, GitHub records visitors’ IP addresses in its server logs to keep the service secure. We don’t receive or use those logs.</p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>The data controller is {{ site.legal.owner }}, sole trader, trading as {{ site.legalName }}, {{ site.legal.address }}, Ireland.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>To see the data held about you, or to ask for it to be corrected or deleted, email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>.</p>
  <p>If you are not happy with how your data is handled, you can complain to the Data Protection Commission at <a href="https://www.dataprotection.ie" rel="noopener">dataprotection.ie</a>.</p>

  <p class="back-home"><a class="btn bv-md" href="/">Back to the home page</a></p>
</div></div>
